### Quick How‑to with the Google Geocoding API

```bash
curl "https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY"
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key. The response will look like the JSON snippet above.

### What this spot is

Those coordinates point to the **Googleplex** – Google’s headquarters in Mountain View, California. It’s a well‑known landmark, so the reverse‑geocode result will almost always return the address “1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA”.

If you need anything else—like converting the coordinates to a different format, or embedding them in a map—just let me know!
